  "texts": [
    "How does a hard kernel turn into fluffy popcorn?",
    "Each kernel has a tough shell that barely lets water through.",
    "Inside is starch and a little water, about fourteen percent.",
    "Heat the kernels in a pot, and the water inside warms up.",
    "Above 100 degrees it becomes steam, but it cannot escape.",
    "Pressure inside climbs to about nine atmospheres.",
    "Meanwhile, the hot steam turns the starch into a soft gel.",
    "At around 180 degrees, the shell finally gives way.",
    "Steam bursts out and the starch puffs up like foam.",
    "The kernel grows up to forty times in volume.",
    "The foam cools fast and sets crispy.",
    "The pop comes from escaping steam, like a champagne cork.",
    "Bulging starch kicks the pot, so the kernel jumps.",
    "Kernels with cracked shells leak steam and never pop.",
    "Follow for more kitchen physics you never noticed!"
  ]
